  "intro": "The Enochian tablets come down in two traditions: John Dee's own records of 1584 and 1587, and the Golden Dawn's tablets, which grew from them. Both are given here. The Golden Dawn's version is the default, here and in the hall diagrams, and Dee's tables, as he recorded them, are here for those who work from Dee alone. Each version below says where it comes from and how it differs from the others.",
  "versions": [
    {
      "id": "gd",
      "title": "The Golden Dawn's",
      "text": "The tablets as the Golden Dawn used them, and the default here. Each square has Regardie's higher letter, which he prefers while allowing both, except where both other Golden Dawn sources print another letter and the Order's names through the square read it too, and in Water's one square of four letters. The other letters any of the three sources prints are kept as second letters. The reversed letters are those the Equinox prints in Enochian, and the sigils are Regardie's, drawn here from his description.",
      "sources": [
