        }
      ],
      "reversed": "Reversed letters: the eight the Equinox prints in Enochian, one or two in each Watchtower.",
      "sigils": "Sigils: Regardie's, which he says are taken from Dee's Sigillum Dei Aemeth.",
      "differs": {
        "regardie": "It is Regardie's print with a few squares chosen otherwise: where both other sources and the Order's names read another letter, and in Water's square of four letters, where it takes the N the others print. It also reverses the letters the Equinox prints in Enochian, which Regardie prints plain.",
        "equinox": "Where Regardie prints two letters it takes the higher, and the Equinox, which prints one, often has the lower. Where Dee's two tables differ, the Equinox mostly has the 1584 letter and this version the 1587 one. Both reverse the same letters.",
        "dee": "It keeps most of Dee's 1584 letters. It differs mostly where the reform of 1587 changed them, for Regardie's higher letters are mostly the 1587 ones: Earth's eighth row above all, which the reform moved one square left. It differs too in a few squares where it has a letter neither of Dee's tables has, it fills the two Fire squares Dee's record leaves empty, and its capitals are Regardie's.",
        "raphael": "The two agree in nearly every letter, since Regardie's higher letters are mostly Raphael's. Most of their differences are of case, for the 1659 print of the 1587 table is set in small letters. Where the letter differs, this version has a letter neither of Dee's tables has, or keeps the 1584 letter, or has p where the 1587 print has x."
      }
    },
