      "differs": {
        "gd": "It is the Golden Dawn's version before its choices: Regardie's higher letter everywhere, even in the few squares where the version takes the letter the other sources and the Order's names read, his y in Water's square of four letters, and nothing reversed.",
        "equinox": "Regardie prints a second letter in many squares and the Equinox one letter a square, often Regardie's lower one. Where Dee's two tables differ, Regardie's higher letter is mostly the 1587 one and the Equinox's the 1584 one.",
        "dee": "Where Dee's two tables differ, Regardie's higher letter is mostly the 1587 one, and his lower often the 1584 one, so his print and Dee's 1584 table differ most where the reform changed the letters. He also has letters in neither of Dee's tables, often look-alikes (l and i, b and l, z and x), and he fills the two Fire squares Dee's record leaves empty.",
        "raphael": "Regardie's higher letters are mostly Raphael's, so the two differ little in letter. They differ in case, since the 1659 print of the 1587 table is set in small letters, and where Regardie has a letter in neither of Dee's tables or keeps a 1584 letter above a 1587 one."
