    {
      "id": "dee",
      "title": "Dee's, 1584",
      "text": "The four tables Edward Kelley dictated to John Dee in Cracow in June 1584, as Dee recorded them and as he corrected them. Kelley was told to write small letters and great, so the capitals are deliberate; here they are Casaubon's type, since the manuscript could not be read. In four squares Dee's record has a letter that every later copy replaces: Dee asked the angel about his corrections, and was told the tables were true and his capitals well corrected. This version takes the corrected letters and keeps the first ones as second letters. Two squares of Fire are empty in every 1584 witness read; they are drawn empty, with Raphael's 1587 letters as second letters.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "work": "casaubon1659",
