        },
        {
          "work": "cottonAppXLVI"
        },
        {
          "work": "sloane3191"
        }
      ],
      "reversed": "Reversed letters: seven of Dee's eight, as modern renderings of the 1587 copies mark them; the eighth, Earth's R, left the table when its row moved. The 1659 print shows the L reversed, and the P as a q.",
      "sigils": "Sigils: none, as for Dee's 1584 table.",
      "differs": {
        "gd": "The Golden Dawn mostly took Raphael's letters as its higher letters, so the two differ little in letter. They differ in case, the 1587 table being printed in small letters, and where the Golden Dawn keeps a 1584 letter, has a letter neither of Dee's tables has, or reads p where this table has x. It has no Tablet of Union.",
        "regardie": "Regardie's higher letters are mostly this table's, so the two differ little in letter, but much in case. Regardie also prints second letters, many of them this table's predecessor's.",
        "equinox": "The Equinox mostly follows the 1584 table where the two of Dee's differ, so it differs from this one in the squares the reform changed, Earth's eighth row above all, and in case.",
        "dee": "It is Dee's 1584 table reformed: Earth's eighth row moved one square left, losing its reversed R and gaining t, Fire's top right corner filled and changed, and a few letters changed elsewhere. It is printed in small letters."
      }
