  "differences": [
    {
      "id": "letters",
      "title": "Letters",
      "text": "Most squares hold the same letter in every version. Where they differ it is usually by a letter that looks alike in a hand or in print (z and x, c and t, n and u, l and i), by u against v, which were one letter in Dee's day, or by a capital.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "work": "regardie1940",
          "page": 270,
