    {
      "id": "earthRow8",
      "title": "The eighth row of Earth",
      "text": "The eighth row of the Earth tablet differs most. The reform of 1587 moved Dee's 1584 row one square to the left, dropping its reversed R and adding a t at the end. Regardie prints both rows, the 1587 one above, and the Golden Dawn's version reads his higher letters; the Equinox and Greer each follow a different mixture of the two.",
