        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "emptyFire",
      "title": "Two empty squares in Fire",
      "text": "In Dee's 1584 record two squares at the top right of the Fire table, row 1 square 12 and row 2 square 11, are empty, printed as dots, and a modern rendering of the Cotton manuscript leaves them empty too. The 1587 table fills them with a and v, and every Golden Dawn source has a letter there. Dee's version leaves them empty and gives the 1587 letters as second letters, and the hall and the image draw them blank.",
      "sources": [
