        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "attributions",
      "title": "Elements and quarters",
      "text": "The Golden Dawn gives each Watchtower an element and a quarter: Air the East, Water the West, Earth the North and Fire the South, and divides each into four lesser angles, one for each element. Giving a whole table one element is the Order's addition: Dee's record gives elements to the angels under each lesser cross, of air, water, earth and fire, and names the tables by the first letters of their middle rows, ORO, MPH, MOR and OIP.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "work": "regardie1940",
          "page": 270,
          "leaf": 262
        },
        {
          "work": "equinox1912",
          "page": 234,
          "leaf": 240
        },
        {
          "work": "casaubon1659",
          "page": 181,
          "leaf": 270
        },
        {
          "work": "casaubon1659",
          "page": 177,
          "leaf": 266
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "sigils",
      "title": "Sigils",
      "text": "Each Golden Dawn Watchtower carries a sigil: a Tau with four flames for Air, a cross potent with figures in its angles for Water, a cross potent for Earth and a circle of twelve rays for Fire. Regardie says they are taken from Dee's Sigillum Dei Aemeth. The Equinox draws them a little differently. Dee's and Raphael's tables are drawn here without them.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "work": "regardie1940",
          "page": 307,
          "leaf": 299
        },
        {
          "work": "equinox1912",
          "plate": "X",
          "leaf": 256
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "colours",
      "title": "Colours and pyramids",
      "text": "The Order painted each tablet in its element's colour and its own angle's letters in the complementary one, the crosses black on white, and the Tablet of Union white with each line in its element's colour. It also treats every square as a truncated pyramid whose sides carry elements, signs, planets and other attributions, as the Equinox draws them.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "work": "regardie1940",
          "page": 274,
          "leaf": 266
        },
        {
          "work": "regardie1940",
          "page": 275,
          "leaf": 267
        },
        {
          "work": "equinox1912",
          "plate": "IV",
          "leaf": 242
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tablets": {
    "earth": {
      "text": "The Watchtower of the North, Earth, in the Golden Dawn's attribution: Dee's MOR, after the first letters of its middle row. Its eighth row is where the versions differ most. In Dee's 1584 record Casaubon prints two marks the readings do not record: a rule under the c of row 12, square 6, and over the V of row 13, square 6; what they mean is unknown, perhaps letters Dee queried. Its Golden Dawn sigil is a cross potent, its arms in four colours.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "work": "regardie1940",
          "page": 272,
          "leaf": 264
        },
        {
          "work": "regardie1940",
          "page": 307,
          "leaf": 299
        },
        {
          "work": "casaubon1659",
          "page": 176,
          "leaf": 265
        },
        {
